WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.480
Stranger Things big bad, Vecna, has joined&nbsp;
the ranks of TV and film's great iconic horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.600
villains, but as scary as he already is, there&nbsp;
were a ton of even more terrifying designs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.040
looks that didn't make the final cut!
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.360
I'm Jan and in this video I'm revealing&nbsp;
and explaining all the horrifying Vecna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.160
designs you never got to see in the show!
This early version of Vecna had an "armoured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:29.680
shell" over his body and face and was inspired&nbsp;
by the prehistoric fish, the Dunkleosteus.
&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.960
This giant fish, which was up to 29&nbsp;
feet long and could weigh over 4 tons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:41.040
had large bony plates that formed its face and&nbsp;
jaws, and like Vecna, was a fearsome predator.
&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.960
The idea behind this original design was that,&nbsp;
over time, living in the Upside Down had hardened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:52.480
and separated pieces of Henry's skin from each&nbsp;
other, forming these tough plates over his body.
&nbsp;

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:56.320
Another iteration of this design&nbsp;
used a spiky version of the armour,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.640
which almost gives him the appearance of&nbsp;
being covered in shards of rock or stone..
&nbsp;

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.560
The designs ended up being rejected as&nbsp;
they were too rigid and didn't allow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.680
for enough of Vecna's expressions&nbsp;
and emotions to come through.
&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.120
This next early design had some&nbsp;
grotesque insect-like arms and legs.
&nbsp;

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.480
The look was inspired by the real-life mantis&nbsp;
and its two large forelegs which have adapted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:24.400
so that the creature can catch and grab its prey.
The arms of this particular Vecna could also split&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.160
open to form claws that he would then use to stab&nbsp;
his victims, something Vecna actually did in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:35.920
final form but with his more human-like claws.
It's a very creepy design that would have fit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.760
well with Henry Creel's love of&nbsp;
spiders and it also reminds me of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.560
Pennywise's spider form in IT Chapter Two.
The issue with it though was that it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.840
have been very hard to achieve practically, given&nbsp;
the extended appendages needed for the villain.
&nbsp;

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.320
The Duffer Brothers were keen that Vecna have a&nbsp;
practical feel about him, and the final version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:59.680
of the villain was all practical makeup and&nbsp;
prosthetics, with just VFX used for his vines. 
&nbsp;

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:05.280
This alternate version of Vecna is much&nbsp;
more alien-like, with some kind of skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:10.240
or webbing growing over and covering his&nbsp;
eyes, making him appear almost blind.
&nbsp;

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:15.280
The thinking behind this look was to give&nbsp;
Vecna more of an extra-terrestrial vibe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:20.000
with the idea being that Henry's time in&nbsp;
the Upside Down had "transformed him into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.440
something closer to a Demogorgon than a human",&nbsp;
according to the artist Michael Maher Jr.
&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.560
This Vecna's look also reminds me of the Pale Man&nbsp;
villain from Pan's Labyrinth who eats children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.080
akin to Vecna who targets&nbsp;
teenagers in Season 4. 
&nbsp;

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.400
Another early idea for Vecna's look&nbsp;
was to have a "patchwork of skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.800
stretched over his gaunt body".
The idea was inspired by Hellraiser&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.280
and I think what they were going for was the&nbsp;
antagonist Frank who comes back from the dead in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:53.200
a degenerated state until his body begins to grow&nbsp;
back flesh and skin as he consumes his victims.
&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.560
An even more gruesome version of this&nbsp;
idea gave Vecna extra pale skin like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.360
a vampire, which seems fitting given the&nbsp;
introduction of the Demobats in Season 4.
&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.200
And his teeth and mouth in this&nbsp;
design gives me some real Cenobite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.000
Chatterer vibes from the Hellraiser franchise.
And there's a touch of the "Demon of the Mind",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.240
Eligos, from Ash vs Evil Dead in this look too.
These designs were inspired by the idea that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:23.200
because Henry had been living in the Upside Down&nbsp;
for so long, his skin had begun to rot away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.520
falling apart in patches, with him&nbsp;
clamping "the skin together to save it".
&nbsp;

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:32.240
In an extra-gross version, the&nbsp;
skin hung over Vecna's jaw, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:37.920
in another the skin had melted over his eyes.
And in this design, whenever Vecna used his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.960
powers, his eyes would cry blood, similar&nbsp;
to what we see happens to Vecna's victims. 
&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.840
The multiple eyes in this design also&nbsp;
remind me of Henry and his love of spiders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.880
creatures which typically have many eyes.
All these designs were rejected because,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.920
similar to the problem with Vecna's armoured&nbsp;
skin, they didn't allow for enough expression.
&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.880
Another idea that was initially explored&nbsp;
was for Henry to become infected with "a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:07.440
type of gangrene" that would corrupt his body.
The thinking was that after years of living in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:12.960
the Upside Down, a mouldy type of rot, together&nbsp;
with vines, had taken hold of Henry's body.
&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:16.640
And the artist describes it as a&nbsp;
type of "tumourous gangrene that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:21.440
would eat away" at Vecna's flesh.
These designs followed a similar idea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.680
the difference being that the rot on&nbsp;
Vecna's body was a bit brighter coloured,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:31.120
and was a type of radioactive rot Henry had&nbsp;
caught from his exposure to the Upside Down.
&nbsp;

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.920
Although these looks were suitably scary for the&nbsp;
villain, the designs were discarded because they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:40.560
didn't disguise Vecna's true identity.
This was crucial so that it would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.400
more difficult to immediately realise&nbsp;
that the seemingly friendly orderly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:48.720
that Eleven first meets at Hawkins Lab&nbsp;
is actually the series' big bad. 
&nbsp;

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:55.200
This alternate design for Vecna emphasises his&nbsp;
asymmetrical look with his over-sized left arm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.560
but with also a giant tentacle attached.
&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:03.600
A particularly weird unused design is&nbsp;
this one where Vecna still had some thin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:09.280
long strands of hair on his head, an idea that was&nbsp;
quickly rejected in all the subsequent designs.
&nbsp;

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.520
This Vecna also had some little spikes&nbsp;
growing out of his shoulders and hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:18.480
and the look of his face reminds me a little&nbsp;
of the serial killer from the movie Smiley.
&nbsp;

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:22.640
I think it's safe to say that most of these&nbsp;
alternate designs for Vecna are even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:27.200
terrifying and unsettling than the already&nbsp;
scary version of the villain we did get. 
&nbsp;

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:32.320
In the end, the more humanoid version they&nbsp;
went for reflects his human origins better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:36.800
together with the elements of the Upside Down&nbsp;
that became part of his body such as roots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.280
vines, and new muscle tissue.
Vecna's red, purple and black colours which are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:46.240
associated with the Upside Down are meant to show&nbsp;
how the alternate dimension took over his body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:52.080
and any human flesh left over is pale because he's&nbsp;
been away from daylight for such a long time.
&nbsp;

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.600
I do want to thank Emmy-nominated artist Michael&nbsp;
Maher Jr for sharing all of these incredible and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.960
original designs for Vecna, which Barrie Gower&nbsp;
and his makeup effects company translated into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:08.400
an amazing on-screen look for the villain.
The prosthetic makeup took between six and seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:13.360
hours every day to apply, meaning that the&nbsp;
makeup team and actor Jamie Campbell Bower's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:18.800
working day began at 2 or 3am so he'd be&nbsp;
ready for shooting later that morning.
&nbsp;

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:24.080
And it then took another hour once filming&nbsp;
was finished each day to take it all off.
&nbsp;

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:29.120
All-in-all, Henry, One and Vecna make an&nbsp;
incredibly compelling central villain in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:34.320
Stranger Things, and if you'd like to learn how&nbsp;
I expect the series to end, tap here to watch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:40.080
my Season 5 theory video and also why Eleven&nbsp;
will end up using time travel to defeat Vecna.
